 "arc": "The cabbage patch: both hands circle around each other in front of the chest, one full scoop per weight shift, while the torso rocks side to side. Captured slow (source about half this length), 3/4 view.\n\nFrame 0 is the top of the scoop — character-right arm raised above shoulder height, weight on the character-right foot. Frames 1-4 bring the hands down and across to waist height as the weight crosses to the character-left foot. Frames 5-9 are the far side: character-left arm up at chest height, hands continuing the circle, weight held on the character-left foot for five frames — the longest single support in the loop.\n\nFrames 11-15 unwind back to the character-right side and re-raise the character-right arm above the shoulder, so frame 15 arrives in frame 0's shape. The seam is clean. The one thing to protect is the continuity of the circle: it never stops or reverses, it only changes which hand leads. This capture has no pilot frames at all — every frame is travel at the same rate, so no single frame should be drawn as a pose.",
